# LINE ENDINGS, DECIDED HERE INSTEAD OF BY WHOEVER CLONES.
#
# Every text file in this repository is stored LF in the index and checked
# out LF, on every platform. That is already true of the index -- `git
# ls-files --eol` reports i/lf for all 151 text files -- but only because
# this machine happens to have core.autocrlf=true, which is a PER-MACHINE
# git setting and not part of the repository at all. A fresh clone on a
# Windows box configured differently would get CRLF working files.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS HERE, SPECIFICALLY. The harnesses do not import the code
# they test; they regex functions out of the source and eval them (the
# fossil development method, see CLAUDE.md). Anchors like /}\n\)\(\);/ and
# the makeDeck extraction in check-route match LF and not CRLF, so a CRLF
# checkout killed check-pool, check-route and check-player with FATAL on
# 2026-08-19. Twelve `.replace(/\r\n/g, '\n')` calls were added afterwards
# and are the only thing standing between a fresh Windows clone and a red
# run. Those calls stay -- they are cheap and they are already written --
# but the guarantee should not rest on somebody remembering to add the
# thirteenth. This file is the gate; the replaces are the belt.
#
# eol=lf rather than plain `text=auto`: text=auto alone normalises the
# INDEX and still hands Windows CRLF in the working tree, which is exactly
# the state the harnesses die in.
* text=auto eol=lf

# BINARY, NAMED RATHER THAN DETECTED. Git's auto-detection gets all 14 of
# them right today (`git ls-files --eol` shows i/-text w/-text), but "right
# by heuristic" and "right by declaration" fail differently: a release zip
# or the essentia wasm blob silently EOL-converted is a corrupt artefact
# that still looks like a file. The extensions actually in the tree are
# .zip .png .wasm .mem; the rest are here so the day one arrives is not the
# day it gets mangled.
*.zip     binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.ico     binary
*.wasm    binary
*.mem     binary
*.onnx    binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
*.ttf     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.flac    binary
*.mp3     binary
*.ogg     binary
*.opus    binary
*.wav     binary
*.m4a     binary
*.aac     binary
